  {
    "episode_id": 72820,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72820.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Oh, I absolutely can. No matter how good the people legislation No matter how well thought out, no matter how agreed to, nonetheless, taking a bill, a statute, and turning it into the rules and regulations and implementing it is always a challenge. My subcommittee chair, men and women, my colleagues on the committee as a whole, stand prepared to work with and to help the administration move some of these rather bold policies changes forward. It will take time, of course, when you're literally stepping away from the old rec payment system and going to what in essence amounts to an insurance-based system when you consolidate the number of conservation programs we are consolidating the changes in the nutrition program food stamps and implementation of the 10 state pilot project for able-bodied adult citizens with work requirement all of those things are going to take some time and effort and we're going to look over their shoulder but there's also can a couple of other things out there that were directly or indirectly related to Farm Bill that require more scrutiny, too. Remember, it's time to reauthorize the language that creates the Commodity Futures Trading Commission. And my good subcommittee chairman, Mr. Conway of Texas, has put a lot of effort into the hearings. Sometime this spring or into the summer, we'll address that. I see how the Senate responds. There were a few issues in the Farm Bill that didn't necessarily come to everybody's satisfaction. I would suspect that there'll be hearings dealing with the country of origin labeling a cool a lot of folks like refer to it uh... that's out there in the mix uh... will be a busy committee for the rest of the year whether it's implementation looking over the shoulder of the department helping encourage the department helping provide guidance through the hearing process or these other issues uh... that uh... command uh... a need for the committee to respond",
