    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "If you address things like the livestock disaster program, where we literally not only provide a safety net for livestock producers moving forward, but we backfill the deficiencies of the previous farm bill, I'd say if I were a stockman in South Dakota, the stuff suffered the massive damages that they had in the early harsh winter weather this season, I think I'd define it as a priority. I know my neighbors in the Southwest who've dealt with drought issues that were not fully funded in the final year of the old farm bill i would like to see that ketchup work done i know the part of the part will prioritize that things as uh... they see fit and as they believe will be the most efficient use of time but uh... if you're a stockman in the decoders if you're a stockman in the in uh... much of the rest of the country they went through the super drought you probably would like to see uh... see that language implemented sooner",
