    "turn_text": "What's a big decision again? It's a big decision. I expect USDA to be putting tools together to help give farmers insights in how to make the decision. I expect land grant universities all across the country to engage in creating models to help provide that guidance. Superficially, I would say, there's probably going to be a pattern there. The revenue option will be used more likely by my friends in the Midwest. where they've got a better soil situation, they've got a more consistent weather situation, where they have the effects of the renewable fuel standard on their core commodity groups. I would expect not every time, but more likely than not, the rest of the country where the weather's patterns are different, where the soil conditions are different, where renewable fuel is not as much of a factor. I would expect them to perhaps be more focused on the price protection, but",
