    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "debate in this Farm Bill. There were those who advocated, well, just give producers both. Just give them the option both. Let them have whatever's the best on any given year. We had to operate within a very tight budget requirement. And ultimately saving in total approximately in comparison to the previous bill, about $23 billion. That required that tough decisions be made. If you gave everyone automatically, whatever the best option was in any given year, that dramatically increased the cost of the commodity title. By giving producers the ability to pick one or the other and stay with their decision, it brought down the overall cost of the commodity title and enabled each option to be more robust, to be better. So if you wanted everything, you were going to get a whole lot less. If you wanted an option where you had to make a choice and it required you to make a choice in the best interest of your farm, Then you made the right choice. You will get substantially a better safety net from it. That's really the bottom line in that decision-making process.",
