    "turn_text": "Congressman, last question and that is about you and your future as a member of Congress from Oklahoma. Your state's very conservative and the compromise action you took to get this bill passed seems to be too far to the left for a sizable portion of your constituents across the border from you in Kansas. Every member of the congressional delegation voted against the bill and the reason seemed to be political cover. You already have a Republican opponent who's expressing very conservative views. Do you think you're going to have a strong challenge in the primary election this spring, partly because of your compromise method on this farm bill?",
